    &lt;p align="left" style="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0.0px;margin-left:0.0px;">
&lt;span style="font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT; font-size:10pt; color:#000000; font-weight:normal;">Link to an optional rating established from a &lt;/span>&lt;span style="font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT; font-size:10pt; color:#000000; font-weight:normal;">predetermined scale and used to evaluate the standing of a t&lt;/span>&lt;span style="font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT; font-size:10pt; color:#000000; font-weight:normal;">erm (vocabulary entry) in the context of a given &lt;/span>&lt;span style="font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT; font-size:10pt; color:#000000; font-weight:normal;">vocabulary.&lt;/span>

    &lt;/p>

    &lt;p align="left" style="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0.0px;margin-left:0.0px;">
&lt;span style="font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT; font-size:10pt; color:#000000; font-weight:normal;">Note that this attribute is labeled status in Section 8.7 of the PDF&amp;#160;specification, termStatus in Section 9.1 of the PDF&amp;#160;and mvfEntryStatus in the XMI. The equivalence of these attributes is assumed for this model.&lt;/span>

    &lt;/p>

    &lt;p>
[Source: &lt;a href="https://www.omg.org/spec/MVF/1.0/Beta1/PDF">www.omg.org/spec/MVF/1.0/Beta1/PDF&lt;/a>]&amp;#160;

    &lt;/p>

